# Mail gateway authorization for the production d4tech.ru server block

The frontend first calls POST /api/auth/mail-session with its normal Bearer token.
The API responds with a signed Secure HttpOnly d4_mail_access cookie. Nginx must
validate that cookie before every Mailcow route by using auth_request.

Add once inside the d4tech.ru server block:

    location = /__d4_mail_auth {
        internal;
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/auth/mail-session/verify;
        proxy_pass_request_body off;
        proxy_set_header Content-Length "";
        proxy_set_header Cookie $http_cookie;
        proxy_set_header X-Original-URI $request_uri;
    }

    location @d4_mail_login_required {
        return 302 https://d4tech.ru/;
    }

Add these two directives to every location that proxies /mail, /SOGo,
/SOGo.woa or /__mailcow/session/logout:

    auth_request /__d4_mail_auth;
    error_page 401 = @d4_mail_login_required;

Important: a location containing an immediate return (for example location =
/mail) completes in the rewrite phase before auth_request. Replace such a return
with try_files to a named redirect location, or protect the destination itself.
The production rollout must test anonymous 401/redirect and authorized access
before removing the rollback copy.
